{# ============================================================================
SOC TRIAGE REPORT (Enterprise Template v2.1)

PURPOSE: Triage packet for SOC analysts + minimal stakeholder clarity.
GOALS:
  (1) Classify TP/FP/Needs Review
  (2) Summarize supporting evidence
  (3) Recommend actions
  (4) Include calibrated ETS multi-horizon multi-track trend context

NON-REDUNDANCY RULE: Each section answers a distinct question; avoid repeating facts.

AI OVERLAY: When ai_overlay is provided, AI insights are interwoven into relevant
sections. AI statements cite evidence IDs where traceable, or are labeled as
HYPOTHESIS/ASSUMPTION when not.

AI OVERLAY SECTION MAPPING:
  Banner      -> tp_fp_likelihood, tp_fp_rationale, model_version
  §1 Summary  -> executive_summary_statements
  §2 Actions  -> next_checks
  §4 Scope    -> scope_interpretation, correlation_insights
  §5 TI       -> tp_fp_evidence_citations, enrichment_interpretation
  §6 Exposure -> exposure_interpretation, exploit_likelihood_assessment
  §7 Trend    -> trend_interpretation, trend_concerns, track_interpretations
  §8 Timeline -> timeline_narrative, attack_chain_hypothesis
  §9 Assess   -> scorecard_explanation, hypotheses, decision_checklist
  §10 Similar -> similar_case_narratives
  §12 Stakeh. -> business_impact_summary, risk_communication
  §13 DataQual-> data_quality_observations, confidence_caveats

DATA STRUCTURE: This template expects `r` (TriageReport) as the top-level object:
  r.signal     - Normalized signal
  r.meta       - Report metadata
  r.ctx        - Signal context (entities, indicators, CVEs)
  r.classification - Classification result with MITRE
  r.forecast   - Multi-track ETS forecasts (rule, ioc, entity)
  r.enrich     - Enrichment bundle (TI, scope, timeline, etc.)
  r.similar_cases - Structured similar cases
  r.recommendations - SOC runbook actions
  r.exec       - Executive summary (optional)

============================================================================ #}

