## 11. Closure Criteria

**Mark as TRUE POSITIVE if**
{% if r.signal.type in ["SIEM_ALERT", "siem_alert", "EDR_DETECTION"] -%}
- Confirmed malicious activity in correlated telemetry tied to the detection.
- Host/user shows compromise indicators OR confirmed exploit attempt.
{% elif r.signal.type in ["IOC", "ioc", "TI_INDICATOR"] -%}
- Indicator confirmed active in environment with malicious context.
- Associated activity indicates compromise or attempted compromise.
{% elif r.signal.type in ["CVE", "cve", "VULNERABILITY_ALERT"] -%}
- CVE is exploitable AND evidence of exploitation attempt or successful exploit.
- Vulnerable asset is exposed AND attacker has access path.
{% elif r.signal.type in ["EMAIL_SECURITY_ALERT"] -%}
- Phishing/malware confirmed delivered AND user interaction occurred.
- Credential theft or malware execution confirmed.
{% elif r.signal.type in ["HUNT", "HUNT_FINDING"] -%}
- Hunt hypothesis confirmed with supporting evidence.
- Malicious activity identified requiring response.
{% elif r.signal.type in ["USER_REPORT", "USER_REPORTED"] -%}
- Reported activity confirmed as malicious.
- Evidence of compromise found on affected systems.
{% else -%}
- Confirmed malicious activity in correlated telemetry tied to the signal/indicator/CVE.
- Host/user shows compromise indicators OR confirmed exploit attempt aligned to telemetry.
{% endif %}

**Mark as FALSE POSITIVE / benign if**
{% if r.signal.type in ["SIEM_ALERT", "siem_alert", "EDR_DETECTION"] -%}
- Activity fully explained by authorized change/maintenance (corroborated).
- Detection is verified non-applicable or benign in this environment (documented).
{% elif r.signal.type in ["IOC", "ioc", "TI_INDICATOR"] -%}
- Indicator is stale/no longer malicious (verified with multiple TI sources).
- Sighting is benign (e.g., security research, sinkhole, CDN).
{% elif r.signal.type in ["CVE", "cve", "VULNERABILITY_ALERT"] -%}
- CVE not exploitable in this configuration (confirmed).
- Compensating controls mitigate the vulnerability (documented).
{% elif r.signal.type in ["EMAIL_SECURITY_ALERT"] -%}
- Email is legitimate (verified sender, expected content).
- No user interaction or malware execution occurred.
{% elif r.signal.type in ["HUNT", "HUNT_FINDING"] -%}
- Hunt hypothesis disproven with evidence.
- Activity explained by legitimate operations.
{% elif r.signal.type in ["USER_REPORT", "USER_REPORTED"] -%}
- Reported activity is legitimate (verified).
- No evidence of compromise found.
{% else -%}
- Activity fully explained by authorized change/maintenance (corroborated).
- Detection/IOC/CVE is verified non-applicable or benign in this environment (documented).
{% endif %}

**Runbook reference:** {{ r.classification.runbook_ref if r.classification.runbook_ref else "RB-GEN-001 Generic Signal Triage" }}

